---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ToolSchema from '../../components/ToolSchema.astro';
---
<Base image="/og/tool-roblox-remote-validator.png" title="Roblox RemoteEvent validator generator" description="Describe what a RemoteEvent receives and get server-side Luau that type-checks, range-checks and rate-limits every argument, so exploiters can't send whatever they want.">
  <ToolSchema />
  <div class="prose" data-pagefind-body>
    <h1>Roblox RemoteEvent validator generator</h1>
    <p class="lede">Exploiters can fire any RemoteEvent with <strong>any arguments</strong>. Describe what your remote should receive, and get the server-side Luau that rejects everything else: wrong types, out-of-range numbers, NaN, huge strings, fake objects and spam.</p>
    <p class="meta">Runs entirely in your browser. The generated pattern is tested against 20+ malicious inputs in the real Luau runtime. Background: <a href="/blog/roblox-remote-events-never-trust-the-client/">never trust the client</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <form class="tool" id="rv">
    <fieldset>
      <legend>Remote</legend>
      <label class="row"><span>RemoteEvent name (in ReplicatedStorage)</span><input type="text" name="remote" value="BuyItem" spellcheck="false" /></label>
      <label class="row"><span>Rate limit (seconds between calls, 0 = none)</span><input type="number" name="rate" value="0.5" min="0" step="0.1" /></label>
    </fieldset>
    <fieldset>
      <legend>Arguments the client sends (after <code>player</code>)</legend>
      <div id="args"></div>
      <button type="button" class="action" id="add">+ Add argument</button>
    </fieldset>
    <button type="submit" class="action">Generate</button>
  </form>

  <div id="errors" aria-live="polite"></div>
  <h2>Server Script</h2>
  <pre class="out"><code id="out"></code></pre>
  <button type="button" class="copy" id="copy">Copy</button>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>What the generated code does</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Treats every client value as <code>unknown</code> and checks its type with <code>typeof()</code> before touching it.</li>
      <li>Numbers: rejects NaN and infinity (both pass naive <code>&lt;</code>/<code>&gt;</code> checks), enforces min/max and whole numbers if needed.</li>
      <li>Strings: rejects empty and over-long values. "Choice" only accepts the listed values.</li>
      <li>Vector3: rejects NaN components and, optionally, positions too far away. Instances: checks the class and that the object is still in the world.</li>
      <li>Optional per-player rate limit, with cleanup when players leave (no memory leak).</li>
      <li>Only then calls <code>handle(...)</code> with properly typed values. That's where your logic goes.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Still your job</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Never accept values the server can work out itself</strong>: prices, damage, rewards. Look them up on the server.</li>
      <li>Check server state inside <code>handle()</code>: does the player own it, can they afford it, are they close enough?</li>
      <li>RemoteFunctions need the same checks, and never call <code>InvokeClient</code> from the server and wait on it.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <template id="row">
    <div class="argrow">
      <input type="text" data-k="name" placeholder="name" aria-label="argument name" spellcheck="false" />
      <select data-k="type" aria-label="argument type">
        <option value="string">string</option>
        <option value="choice">choice (one of a list)</option>
        <option value="integer">integer</option>
        <option value="number">number</option>
        <option value="boolean">boolean</option>
        <option value="Vector3">Vector3</option>
        <option value="Instance">Instance</option>
      </select>
      <input type="text" data-k="options" placeholder="allowed values, comma-separated" aria-label="allowed values" />
      <input type="number" data-k="maxLength" placeholder="max length" aria-label="max length" />
      <input type="number" data-k="min" placeholder="min" aria-label="minimum" />
      <input type="number" data-k="max" placeholder="max" aria-label="maximum" />
      <input type="number" data-k="maxMagnitude" placeholder="max distance" aria-label="max magnitude" />
      <input type="text" data-k="className" placeholder="class, e.g. BasePart" aria-label="class name" />
      <button type="button" class="code-copy remove" aria-label="remove argument">✕</button>
    </div>
  </template>
  <p class="meta tool-feedback">Found a bug or a wrong result? <a href="/contact/">Tell me</a>, or <a href="https://github.com/realFinDev/realfin-site/issues" rel="nofollow">open an issue on GitHub</a>.</p>


  <script is:inline src="/tools/roblox-remote.js"></script>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var form = document.getElementById('rv'), argsEl = document.getElementById('args'), tpl = document.getElementById('row');
      var SHOW = { string: ['maxLength'], choice: ['options', 'maxLength'], integer: ['min', 'max'], number: ['min', 'max'], boolean: [], Vector3: ['maxMagnitude'], Instance: ['className'] };
      function sync(row) {
        var t = row.querySelector('[data-k=type]').value;
        ['options', 'maxLength', 'min', 'max', 'maxMagnitude', 'className'].forEach(function (k) {
          row.querySelector('[data-k=' + k + ']').hidden = SHOW[t].indexOf(k) === -1;
        });
      }
      function addRow(v) {
        var row = tpl.content.firstElementChild.cloneNode(true);
        Object.keys(v || {}).forEach(function (k) { var i = row.querySelector('[data-k=' + k + ']'); if (i) i.value = v[k]; });
        row.querySelector('[data-k=type]').addEventListener('change', function () { sync(row); });
        row.querySelector('.remove').addEventListener('click', function () { row.remove(); gen(); });
        argsEl.appendChild(row); sync(row);
      }
      function gen() {
        var args = Array.prototype.map.call(argsEl.children, function (row) {
          var a = {}; row.querySelectorAll('[data-k]').forEach(function (i) { if (!i.hidden) a[i.dataset.k] = i.value; }); return a;
        });
        var r = window.RobloxRemote.generate({ remote: form.elements.namedItem('remote').value, rateLimit: form.elements.namedItem('rate').value, args: args });
        var err = document.getElementById('errors');
        err.innerHTML = '';
        if (!r.ok) {
          var ul = document.createElement('ul');
          r.errors.forEach(function (e) { var li = document.createElement('li'); li.className = 'warn'; li.textContent = e; ul.appendChild(li); });
          err.appendChild(ul);
          return;
        }
        document.getElementById('out').textContent = r.code;
      }
      document.getElementById('add').addEventListener('click', function () { addRow({ type: 'string', maxLength: 50 }); });
      form.addEventListener('submit', function (e) { e.preventDefault(); gen(); });
      form.addEventListener('change', gen);
      document.getElementById('copy').addEventListener('click', function () {
        var b = this; navigator.clipboard && navigator.clipboard.writeText(document.getElementById('out').textContent).then(function () { b.textContent = 'Copied'; setTimeout(function () { b.textContent = 'Copy'; }, 1200); });
      });
      addRow({ name: 'itemName', type: 'choice', options: 'Sword, Shield', maxLength: 20 });
      addRow({ name: 'amount', type: 'integer', min: 1, max: 99 });
      gen();
    })();
  </script>
</Base>
<style is:global>
  .argrow { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; align-items: center; padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--border); }
  .tool .argrow input, .tool .argrow select { font: inherit; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text); background: var(--bg); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px; padding: 4px 7px; min-width: 0; }
  .argrow input[data-k=name] { width: 9em; }
  .argrow input[type=number] { width: 7em; }
  .argrow input[data-k=options] { flex: 1 1 14em; }
  .argrow .remove { position: static; }
  .tool input[type=text], .tool input[type=number] { font: inherit; color: var(--text); background: var(--bg); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px; padding: 4px 8px; }
  #rv > .action { margin-bottom: 8px; }
</style>
